{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_fault_f67_2_chain_drops_a_findable_channel_f67_2", "label": "Fault F67.2 \u2014 the sealed chain drops a findable d channel at Z=51", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F67.2-CHAIN-DROPS-A-FINDABLE-CHANNEL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f67_2_chain_drops_a_findable_channel_class_c_z51_5d", "label": "CLASS C at Z=51 5d", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F67.2-CHAIN-DROPS-A-FINDABLE-CHANNEL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "log(nrm) goes negative inside the node-correct window, with two sign changes in [-0.0598,-0.0373]: the two-node 5d state the label demands is present, normalisable and findable, and the chain returned the one-node state below the window. Whether it disturbs the ordering cannot be read off an eigenvalue window, because D is a total-energy difference \u2014 settling it needs one solve no filed prediction covers, and 'surprising' is not a score."}, {"id": "recovered_fault_f67_2_chain_drops_a_findable_channel_fail_set_not_unfindable", "label": "The chain's `fail` set is not a set of unfindable channels", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/FAULT-F67.2-CHAIN-DROPS-A-FINDABLE-CHANNEL.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "s66 measured ten cells out of a sealed population of 162 d-channel node-count failures and concluded reading (2) was refuted across a hundred protons. The eleventh cell measured, the first atom outside that set on the pre-collapse side, is CLASS C. The score stands over its own ten cells; the generalisation does not. Until the 162 are measured, 'node-count failure' means 'this solver did not find it', not 'the field does not carry it findably'."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_